{"name":"Blissful Serenity","hex":"#eaeed8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blissful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extremely happy; full of joy; experiencing, indicating, causing, or characterized by bliss.","Blessed; glorified."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blissful"},{"term":"serenity","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being serene; calmness; peacefulness.","A lack of agitation or disturbance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/serenity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blissful","blocks":[{"text":"Blissful is the second album by drummer Hamid Drake and his group Bindu. It was recorded on July 12 and 13, 2007, at Soma Electronic Music Studios in Chicago, Illinois, and was issued on CD in 2008 by Rogueart. On the album, Drake is joined by vocalist Dee Alexander, guitarists Joe Morris and Jeff Parker, and double bassists Josh Abrams and William Parker. Lyrics were written by the 18th-century poet Ramprasad Sen, and were excerpted from Mother of the Universe: Visions of the Goddess and Tantric Hymns of Enlightenment by Lex Hixon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Hamid_Drake_Blissful.jpg/330px-Hamid_Drake_Blissful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blissful","wikidata":"Q125820751"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"blissful":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-blissful.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/85/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-blissful.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-blissful.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/85/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-blissful.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-bli